I built ValueGrowAGarden (<a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;valuegrowagarden.com&#x2F;" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;valuegrowagarden.com&#x2F;</a>
) for players trading items in the Roblox game “Grow a Garden.”<p>What it does<p>Live value list for pets&#x2F;crops with median, P10–P90 range, sample count, and last-updated time<p>“Win&#x2F;Fair&#x2F;Lose” checker to sanity-check a trade in seconds<p>Transparent methodology page and a simple form for players to submit recent trades&#x2F;screenshots<p>Why
Trading values move fast during events and updates. Most lists are either stale or opaque. I wanted something lightweight, data-driven, and easy to verify.<p>How it works (high level)<p>Collect recent trade samples from community submissions and public evidence<p>Clean data (filter obvious outliers&#x2F;manipulation)<p>Compute robust stats (median + P10–P90 band) and show confidence via sample size<p>Roadmap<p>Item history charts and alerts for big moves<p>Public API for bots&#x2F;tools<p>Better handling of thin-liquidity items and mutation&#x2F;ability edge cases<p>Ask<p>Are the stats and UI helpful when you’re mid-trade?<p>Any heuristics you use that I should encode?<p>Ideas to reduce manipulation without hiding the method?<p>Note: Unofficial fan-made site; not affiliated with the game or its developers.
